    "updated_at": "2025-08-30T11:29:00Z",
    "body": "> @noamr Ah, gotcha. Yeah, I think the streaming model makes sense. We may need to do this anyway for SVG, as there's an open question how to handle those (they can be animated, but figuring our their overall duration etc might even be NP-complete).\n> \n> Not showing seeking controls to users may help, though there is always the JS API for seeking…\n\nThe JS API for seeking also relies on the \"seekable ranges\" concept in media elements so I think a solution can be found for this as well.\n\nNote that also rewinding a big GIF can be really costly even if it's already downloaded as it practically needs to be played from the start... Perhaps some optimizations are possible for this but my point is that the larger the GIF, the harder it is to treat it like a normal video without performance and UX implications.",
