    "updated_at": "2025-09-01T13:40:37Z",
    "body": "Apologies if this is already touched on somewhere but something else that needs to be considered is the lack of alt attribute support on video elements. Today a gif in an `<img>` can be easily expressed to assistive tech, videos don't have this. While this might make sense for more traditional video content where a simple alt cannot feasibly convey the information. If video is going to support the use case of stuff like a gif meme or an animated emoji type content, you probably do want an alt.\n\nAdding alt directly to video might not be great idea though as it might push people towards a lazy \"oh we'll just alt that video\" rather than correctly captioning.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
